+ * The provider's own size for the prefix of one live chain, taken from the last
+ * turn the provider actually sized.
+ *
+ * A provider bills one request against the model window and reports the count
+ * back on the response that request produced, so that response's `usage` is the
+ * only byte-faithful ruler for the messages it carried. The local tokenizer
+ * cannot stand in: it must COUNT opaque reasoning payloads (Anthropic signed
+ * thinking blocks) to approach billing at all, but their local byte size
+ * diverges wildly from the provider's charge, so tokenizing them overstates a
+ * thinking-heavy chain several-fold (the incident's real 378k-token request
+ * measured 630k locally) while dropping them understates it (322k). The
+ * attested count carries the provider's own charge for those payloads.
+ *
+ * `coveredMessages` is the index of the message that usage arrived with: the
+ * request which produced it carried every message before it (with this chain's
+ * own system prompt and tools), so only the messages from that index on are
+ * estimated locally.
+ */
+interface ProviderInputAttestation {
+	tokens: number;
+	coveredMessages: number;
